 shown as \"Divide Curve Stats\".\n- **Inputs:** `Curve` and `Count` (default 10).\n- **Outputs:** `Points` (list of points) and `Length` (total curve length), returned as a named tuple.\n\nChoices I made without asking:\n\n- **Point count:** `Count` is the number of segments, so the output has `Count + 1` points, including both ends. This matches Grasshopper's Divide Curve behaviour. If you want only the interior division points, that is a one-line change.\n- **Validation:** a null curve or `Count < 1` throws, which Betta shows as an error.\n- **Division:** `Curve.DivideByCount` returns curve parameters, so each one is converted with `PointAt`.\n\nI did not run the component in Grasshopper, only the build. The project is not a git repository, so I did not commit.","ttft_ms":2229,"type":"result","duration_ms":25915,"uuid":"b09cd97c-686d-43b1-9578-2bff5528a1b4","ttft_stream_ms":1796,"time_to_request_ms":328,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":91,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":20,"input_hooks":13,"conversation_append":1,"tool_pool_refresh":5,"init_message":129,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":5,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":2,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":8,"query_setup":2,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":23,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":8},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":131,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":423,"time_to_request_major_faults":9350,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"skill_listing","slowest_producer_ms":6,"cpu_ms":15,"major_faults":826,"setup_ms":2,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":9,"ambient_wait_ms":5,"render_ms":2,"producers":43,"token_counts":0},"tool_schema_build_detail":{"betas_ms":0,"waits_ms":1,"placement_ms":1,"render_ms":21,"after_ms":0,"other_ms":0,"tools":15,"new_schemas":15},"message_normalization_detail":{"before_ms":0,"normalize_ms":2,"images_ms":0,"post_pr